{
  "name": "Check QR codes and barcodes in label images against an expected value",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nThis workflow helps print, packaging and labeling teams confirm that every label carries the right code before it ships. It reads each image file you name, decodes its QR codes and barcodes on this n8n instance with the open-source QR Code & Barcode Scanner engine, and compares the decoded texts with the value you expect. Each image ends in one branch: **Expected value found**, **Wrong value**, **No code found** or **Unreadable image**, with the file name and what was read. Nothing is uploaded to another service, and decoded links are never opened.\n\n### Setup\n1. Self-host n8n and install the community node `@qrcode-ai-com/n8n-nodes-qrcode-barcode-scanner` 0.1.0 under **Settings**, **Community nodes** ([installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation-and-management)). n8n Cloud cannot install it. Tested on n8n 2.48.7.\n2. Put the label images (PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF) in a folder n8n may read. The default is `~/.n8n-files`; `N8N_RESTRICT_FILE_ACCESS_TO` changes it.\n3. In **Settings**, set `expectedText` to the value the labels must carry and `imageFiles` to a path or a pattern such as `/home/node/.n8n-files/labels/*.png`.\n4. Click **Execute workflow**.\n\n### Customization\nChoose the **Full** profile in the scan node to also score how well each QR code scans. Connect a spreadsheet, a chat message or a ticket after the branches you care about.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "a8aa6315-fc9d-57fe-861a-a0d866f03f63",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -580,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Choose the label images\nSettings holds the two values to change. The file step reads every image that matches `imageFiles`.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "7a078ddc-ed0b-5a76-a115-761b0adfe214",
      "name": "Choose the label images",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Scan each image\nDecodes every QR code and barcode locally. A corrupt file takes the error output, so the run goes on.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "06083fae-e039-58b5-ac8c-c4488cdf491c",
      "name": "Scan each image",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        600,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Sort the results\nEach image takes one branch, with its file name and the texts read. Connect your own report or alert after them.",
